## T11 â€” Provider adapters
Reasoning: Four providers with different wire protocols must produce the same draft schema, never retry silently, and 
classify rejections only by documented signals. T8 (TRACK) capability matrix 
`src/lib/meeting-notes/ai/capabilities.ts` holds models, reasoning wire fragments, budgets, base URLs (Kimi 
api.moonshot.ai, GLM api.z.ai), and rejection combos; GLM supports only `json_object`, so its draft must be validated 
after parsing.
Task: Server-only adapters: Anthropic via `@anthropic-ai/sdk`, OpenAI via `openai`, Kimi and GLM via the OpenAI SDK 
with their OpenAI-compatible base URLs; SDK retries disabled (`maxRetries: 0`); each sends only the matrix's valid 
parameters for the chosen model and reasoning level; output requested and validated against one draft schema (summary 
sections, â‰¤100 items with description and assignee name as written); malformed/truncated output is a failure; an 
input-size preflight against the model's context/output budget refuses oversize transcripts before any request; 
provider errors are mapped to sanitized messages (no key, no transcript) and classified as pre-processing rejection 
only per the matrix. A server-only base-URL override selects the fake server; it is ignored and logged as refused when 
`NODE_ENV=production`, and no client input can set it.
