## T12 â€” Processing and Apply flow on the server
Reasoning: Joins admission, dispatch, draft, authorization rechecks, and atomic Apply â€” the heart of FR-015â€“FR-021 
â€” and owns every dispatch-dependent check (review P2â€“P5). Apply appends items as T2 (TRACK) established: call 
`private.meeting_note_lock_for_change(note_id, <NOT_FOUND token>)` (actor KEY SHARE â†’ note FOR UPDATE; returns 
can_edit, note_revision), insert with creator snapshots and `assignee_name` whenever `assignee_id` is set; the item 
insert trigger raises 22023 MEETING_NOTE_ITEM_LIMIT_REACHED past 100 and the whole Apply rolls back; READ COMMITTED.
Task: A start route that, in order: verifies the ticket signature and the 24 h expiry of the ticket and its embedded 
key before any lookup (expired â†’ rejected, no dispatch, even without records; a client-supplied key differing from 
the ticket's is rejected); compares the ticket's user/company/note with the authenticated application user; calls T9's 
admission RPC, which re-authorizes current membership and editor rights before anything else (existing operation â†’ 
returns its pending/final/"discarded" status without dispatch, even if settings changed since; new operation â†’ 
current membership, editor rights, and current settings revision required, stale revision â†’ refused with the new 
provider name); runs T11's size preflight and, when it refuses or the client cancels before sending, settles the 
operation as never dispatched (released); otherwise dispatches once via T11 with the admitted snapshot, key, and 
transcript; resolves suggested names locally (exact full name, else unique first name, case/accent-insensitive, 
current members only); rechecks membership and note existence before returning; honors client abort (operation 
"discarded") with best-effort outbound abort; and settles usage. An `authenticated`-granted Apply RPC accepts the 
edited summary and accepted items only at the draft's source revision, rechecks rights in the transaction, marks 
suggestions duplicating existing items, appends accepted items under T2's shared per-note lock and capacity, writes 
the summary, and creates one version â€” or changes nothing.
Done when: Processing and Apply satisfy FR-015â€“FR-021 against the fake provider, including every dispatch-dependent 
usage, replay, and authorization outcome.
