1:-- Phase 6 T8: company AI settings with a server-only encrypted key
2:-- (spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes; SPEC FR-024, BR-009, AC-017, AC-023).
3:-- Depends on the baseline (companies, users, private.is_company_member) and on
4:-- the supabase_vault extension in schema `vault` (0.3.1 locally and on
5:-- vhabpcoyypobgasacsko, read-only check 2026-10-13).
6:--
7:-- Objects:
8:--   * public.meeting_note_ai_settings — one row per company (company_id PK →
9:--     companies ON DELETE CASCADE): provider (anthropic/openai/kimi/glm),
10:--     model, reasoning_level, daily_limit 1–200, revision (bumped by every
11:--     save), updated_by_user_id (users.id, ON DELETE SET NULL) +
12:--     updated_by_name snapshot, updated_at, key_last_four. A company without a
13:--     row is "not configured" with the default limit 20 (read side, app code).
14:--     NO key material and NO secret reference live in this table: the key is
15:--     a Vault secret named 'meeting_notes_ai_key:<company_id>' (vault.secrets
16:--     has a unique name index), located by that name only inside the
17:--     SECURITY DEFINER functions below. Members therefore read every column of
18:--     the row without learning anything usable against the key.
19:--   * Grants: authenticated SELECT only, rows of its own company
20:--     (private.is_company_member: users.supabase_uid = auth.uid()); anon
21:--     nothing; service_role SELECT only; no INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE for
22:--     any client role — the save RPC is the only write path. The table is not
23:--     added to any publication (supabase_realtime is not FOR ALL TABLES), and
24:--     vault.secrets / vault.decrypted_secrets keep their extension grants
25:--     (postgres, service_role; nothing for anon/authenticated).
26:--   * public.save_meeting_note_ai_settings(p_actor_user_id uuid,
27:--     p_company_id uuid, p_expected_revision bigint, p_provider text,
28:--     p_model text, p_reasoning_level text, p_daily_limit integer,
29:--     p_api_key text) RETURNS jsonb — service_role only. Called by the
30:--     /api/companies/ai-settings route AFTER it authorized the session user as
31:--     an admin of that company; p_actor_user_id is that server-derived
32:--     users.id. One transaction (READ COMMITTED), lock order (PLAN lock order
33:--     rule): (1) actor users row FOR KEY SHARE — blocks the member-removal and
34:--     role-change RPCs (they lock users FOR UPDATE) and does not conflict with
35:--     presence's NO KEY UPDATE writes; (2) the company's settings row FOR
36:--     UPDATE (or, on a first save, the INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING that
37:--     creates it; its FK check takes the company row FOR KEY SHARE, after the
38:--     users row, as every product RPC orders users → company); (3) only then
39:--     re-verify that the locked actor row is an admin of p_company_id. A
40:--     removal/demotion that committed first is seen by the locking read and
41:--     refuses the save (nothing changes); a save that holds the lock first
42:--     makes the removal wait until it commits (no cycle: the save never waits
43:--     for a lock the removal holds). Then: revision check (stale →
44:--     P0001 MEETING_NOTE_AI_SETTINGS_STALE_REVISION, DETAIL
45:--     {"current_revision": n|null}), validation (provider enum; model/reasoning
46:--     shape — the curated per-provider lists are enforced by the route from
47:--     the server capability matrix; limit 1–200; key printable ASCII 8–512, no
48:--     whitespace; first save requires a key, and keeping the key requires a
49:--     stored secret), write, Vault secret created or
50:--     replaced IN THE SAME TRANSACTION (vault.create_secret /
51:--     vault.update_secret), key_last_four set, revision + 1. Returns masked
52:--     metadata only (never the key). Exception messages are fixed tokens and
53:--     never contain parameter values.
54:--   * public.read_meeting_note_ai_key(p_company_id uuid) RETURNS jsonb —
55:--     service_role only; {revision, provider, model, reasoning_level,
56:--     daily_limit, api_key} from one snapshot, or NULL when not configured.
57:--     For server code that has already authorized the user (T9 admission).
58:--   * private.meeting_note_ai_secret_name(uuid) — the secret name (no grants).
59:--   * private.delete_meeting_note_ai_secret() + AFTER DELETE trigger: when a
60:--     settings row is deleted (company deletion cascades), its Vault secret is
61:--     deleted in the same transaction — no readable orphan remains.
62:--   Every function: owner postgres, SET search_path = '', schema-qualified,
63:--   REVOKE ALL FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated, service_role, then EXECUTE
64:--   only to service_role for the two RPCs (none for the private helpers).
65:--
66:-- Error tokens (message = token; SQLSTATE):
67:--   42501 MEETING_NOTE_AI_SETTINGS_FORBIDDEN (actor missing, not in the
68:--         company, or not an admin — evaluated on the locked row)
69:--   P0001 MEETING_NOTE_AI_SETTINGS_STALE_REVISION (DETAIL current_revision)
70:--   22023 MEETING_NOTE_AI_SETTINGS_INVALID_ARGUMENT (null actor/company),
71:--         MEETING_NOTE_AI_PROVIDER_INVALID, MEETING_NOTE_AI_MODEL_INVALID,
72:--         MEETING_NOTE_AI_REASONING_INVALID, MEETING_NOTE_AI_DAILY_LIMIT_INVALID,
73:--         MEETING_NOTE_AI_KEY_REQUIRED, MEETING_NOTE_AI_KEY_INVALID
74:--
75:-- Rollback (order: FIRST roll the application back to a build without the AI
76:-- settings route/section, THEN run this SQL). It deletes every company's AI
77:-- settings and their Vault secrets (keys are lost; admins re-enter them after
78:-- a re-apply):
79:--   begin;
80:--   drop function if exists public.save_meeting_note_ai_settings(uuid, uuid, bigint, text, text, text, integer, 
text);
81:--   drop function if exists public.read_meeting_note_ai_key(uuid);
82:--   delete from public.meeting_note_ai_settings;  -- the trigger deletes each secret
83:--   delete from vault.secrets where name like 'meeting\_notes\_ai\_key:%';  -- orphans, if any
84:--   drop table if exists public.meeting_note_ai_settings;
85:--   drop function if exists private.delete_meeting_note_ai_secret();
86:--   drop function if exists private.meeting_note_ai_secret_name(uuid);
87:--   commit;
